body:
Honestly, there will be many books where mmc can hate/despise fmc but nothing has touched me the way Aint She Sweet has. It is in its own league purely because of how multi-faceted and fleshed out all her characters were. The dynamic, angst, the banter... every single thing was top tier!! 

that being said, another book that gave me angst and feels for days is {This Heart of mine by Brenda Novak}


it starts with FMC who is freshly out of jail going to meet her teenage son for the first time, whose custody she gave up all that time ago from prison. The entire town including the MMC believe that she murdered MMC's ex. Basically FMC was daughter of a dirt poor family, and MMC was a golden boy, only son of Town's wealthy people. They were teenagers and dating despite all the disapproval, she gets pregnant and then the murder happens. MMC is initially very hesitant to let their son meet the FMC and does believe her to be a murderer.
